.TH OTOP 1 "August 2026" "otop 1.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
otop \- htop/btop for Odoo: terminal monitor for Odoo workers, PostgreSQL and server resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otop
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otop
is a compact, interactive terminal monitor for servers running Odoo. It shows
server load, the Odoo worker processes of each configured instance, the slowest
and heaviest routes, storage (total disk first, then database, filestore and
other), PostgreSQL activity, disk I/O and network throughput.
.PP
Cheap metrics refresh every couple of seconds; expensive ones (filestore
directory size, database size, table sizes) are cached and refreshed on much
slower schedules. otop runs as a single process: no daemon, no web server, no
external services.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file. Without it otop looks at
.BR $OTOP_CONFIG ,
.IR ~/.config/otop/config.yaml ", then " /etc/otop/config.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instance " " \fIKEY\fR
Instance to display first. Defaults to the first configured instance.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Refresh interval for cheap metrics.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-once
Print one snapshot as plain text and exit. Useful over SSH, in scripts and in
cron.
.TP
.B \-\-width \fICOLUMNS\fR
Line width for \fB\-\-once\fR. Defaults to the terminal width.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B r
Refresh now, including the cached filestore and database sizes.
.TP
.BR l ", " s
Switch to the LIVE or STAGING instance. Any instance can also be selected by
its position with the number keys, or cycled with \fBTab\fR.
.TP
.B p
Pause and resume sampling.
.TP
.B t
Sort the ROUTES table: total time, slowest, average, calls.
.TP
.B ?
Help, including the meaning of every status marker.
.SH WORKER STATUS
A worker is reported
.B BUSY
when it owns an established connection on the Odoo HTTP port, or when it has an
active PostgreSQL query. That is an observation, not an inference from CPU use.
Values that could only be approximated are prefixed with
.BR ~ .
.PP
Because sampling happens every couple of seconds, a worker serving very short
requests is often caught idle. The
.B BUSY%
column and the
.B AVG
counter give the share of recent samples in which each worker was busy; use
them, not the instantaneous count, to judge saturation.
.B QUEUED
is the kernel's accept queue on the HTTP port: connections that no worker has
picked up yet.
.PP
Reading a worker's sockets requires running as root or as the Odoo user;
otherwise otop falls back to a CPU-based approximation and says so.
.SH ROUTES
The
.B ROUTES
panel tails the instance's own Odoo log file, which carries one line per
finished request with its SQL query count, its SQL time and its remaining
(Python) time. Requests are grouped by
.IR model.method
for RPC calls and by URL otherwise, with ids and asset hashes folded to
.BR * ,
over a rolling window
.RB ( routes_window ,
15 minutes by default).
.PP
The log path is taken from
.I odoo.conf
or from the running master's
.B \-\-logfile
argument; an instance that logs to standard output or the journal has no route
statistics, and the panel says so rather than showing an empty table. Requests
killed by
.B limit_time_real
or
.B limit_time_cpu
never reach the logger and can therefore be missing from the table entirely.
Timings are Odoo-internal and exclude the proxy, the network and the browser.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/otop/config.yaml
Configuration: one entry per Odoo instance, each usually just pointing at that
instance's own odoo.conf.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/otop/config.example.yaml
Documented example configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error, unknown instance, or no terminal (use \fB\-\-once\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR htop (1),
.BR atop (1),
.BR iotop (8),
.BR top (1)
